# In my enable_raw(): r.c_oflag&=~OPOST; tcsetattr(STDIN_FILENO, ...)
# Since STDIN and STDOUT are the same fd in a TTY, this disables OPOST for both
# But in a PTY test where stdin=slave and stdout=slave, same fd, so OPOST is disabled!

# But original also disables OPOST (it's FTXUI, uses same raw mode approach)
# So why does original get \r\r\n and mine gets \r\n?

# Let me check what the original writes: does it write \r\n or \n or \r\r\n?
# If OPOST is disabled, no translation. So:
# Original must write \r\r\n explicitly
# Mine writes \r\n

# So I need to change my line endings from \r\n to \r\r\n? OR does FTXUI not disable OPOST?

# Actually wait - let me check: FTXUI puts terminal in raw mode INCLUDING OPOST disabled
# With OPOST disabled, the program must send explicit \r\n for each line
# My program sends \r\n which is correct
# But original sends \r\r\n?

# Let me check by looking at the FTXUI source behavior...
# Actually, FTXUI DOES NOT disable OPOST! Let me check what it does:
# FTXUI raw mode setup might only disable ECHO/ICANON/ISIG but NOT OFLAG!

# The double \r\r\n would make sense if OPOST is NOT disabled:
# Program writes \r\n, but since LF is still processed by ONLCR, \n -> \r\n
# Total: \r + \r\n = \r\r\n

